<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sichuan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sichuan is a province of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, centred on a fertile basin. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> it was an important economic region where early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a> developed. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> refer to military campaigns involving Sichuan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sichuan.jpg" alt="Sichuan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: chensiyuan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1_huanglong_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
